-- title:
--   Zusatz: no extreme supports iff $0$ is a strictly positive combination of $S$
-- statement:
--   Let $S \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n$ be a finite non-degenerate point system. Then $S$ has no extreme support (case b) of the Hauptsatz) if and only if the origin is representable by $S$ with all coefficients strictly positive:
--   $$0 = \sum_{s \in S} c_s\, s \qquad \text{with } c_s > 0 \text{ for every } s \in S .$$
--
--   The Zusatz gives a checkable criterion for the case in which the cone generated by $S$ is the whole space. Weyl uses it in §4 II to show that the dual system of a bounded region is non-degenerate.
--
--   (Weyl: "Der Fall b), in welchem keine extremen Stützen vorhanden sind, kann dadurch gekennzeichnet werden, daß die Null darstellbar ist: 0 = λa + μb + ⋯ mit Koeffizienten λ, μ, ⋯, die alle wirklich positiv (nicht Null) sind.")
--
--   **Formalization Note** Non-degeneracy of $S$ is the standing hypothesis of the Hauptsatz, of which the Zusatz is an addendum; without it the equivalence fails (e.g. $S = \{e_1, -e_1\} \subseteq \mathbb{R}^2$).
-- source:
--   Weyl, Elementare Theorie der konvexen Polyeder, Comment. Math. Helv. (1935), pp. 294–295, §2, Zusatz

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_NonDegenerate
import Definitions.Def_WeylPolyhedra_Shared_IsExtremeSupport

namespace WeylPolyhedra.Polyhedron

/-- Weyl (1935), §2, pp. 294–295, Zusatz (to the Hauptsatz): for a finite non-degenerate point
system `S ⊆ ℝⁿ`, `S` has no extreme support (case b) of the Hauptsatz) if and only if `0` is
representable by `S` with every coefficient strictly positive:
`0 = ∑_{s ∈ S} c_s s` with `c_s > 0` for all `s ∈ S`. -/
theorem zusatz {n : ℕ} (S : Finset (Fin n → ℝ)) (hS : Shared.NonDegenerate S) :
    (¬ ∃ α : Fin n → ℝ, Shared.IsExtremeSupport S α) ↔
      ∃ c : (Fin n → ℝ) → ℝ, (∀ s ∈ S, 0 < c s) ∧ (0 : Fin n → ℝ) = ∑ s ∈ S, c s • s := by sorry

end WeylPolyhedra.Polyhedron
